>warning, etc.)  You get it when you die, but I can't find a way to
>display it in the game (seems like "Player's Handbook" material to me).
> Or is there some magic item or tool that reveals this?

Wands and potions of enlightenment will tell you this.

>(b) How do you tunnel through walls?  Do you need a tool to do that?

Pick axes, dwarven mattocks, and wands of digging. Or, polymorph into an
Umber Hulk or Rock Mole. Xorns can walk through walls but leave no tunnel
behind.

>(c) On a related note...I take it you can push boulders but not pull
>them...correct?  Periodically I'll be going down a hallway and come to
>a boulder...sometimes I can't push it or there's a monster on the other
>side.  Is it possible to get stuck in the game (i.e., no down
>staircase) because of a boulder?

I don't know if it is forbidden by code, but I've never yet had the stairs
blocked off by unmoveable boulders. In addition to smashing the boulder
(Pick Axe, Mattock, Wand of Striking), you can use thrown weapons to pelt
things on the other side and kill them.

